\image(figures/sequence_vae_method.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The same decoder weights support two prefix policies. Teacher reconstruction is conditioned on the full-sentence posterior and observed previous tokens; free generation has no target-prefix input.)
\alttext(A full sentence supplies a masked encoder, Gaussian posterior and explicit sampled code. The code initializes two views of the same decoder: one receives true prefixes, while the other feeds emitted tokens back and pads after EOS.)

> A seven-step sentence by hand

Use “a red circle moves left [eos]” with a final PAD. Its targets are
[3,5,8,11,13,2,0]; its decoder inputs must be [1,3,5,8,11,13,2]. Prefix construction shifts
the targets, rather than passing the current token. The EOS target is scored, while the final
PAD target contributes exactly zero. A decoder still updates on that final EOS prefix input;
its raw final scores exist even though the corresponding target loss is masked.

For a zero-parameter model with uniform 19-way logits and zero posterior/noise, KL is 0 and
sentence NLL is 6 log 19. This controlled arithmetic example is independent of the fitted model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sequence_vae_prefixes.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n              = dm::nn;
  namespace m              = n::models;
  const auto        t      = n::DType::Float64;
  const auto        tokens = n::from_vector(std::vector<int>{3, 5, 8, 11, 13, 2, 0}, {1, 7});
  n::ParameterStore p(3109, t);
  m::SequenceVariationalAutoencoder(p, tokens, n::zeros({1, 4}, t));
  p.unflatten(std::vector<double>(p.count(), 0));
  const auto out = m::SequenceVariationalAutoencoder(p, tokens, n::zeros({1, 4}, t));
  if (std::abs(out.nll.item() - 6 * std::log(19.)) > 1e-12 || out.kl.item() != 0)
    return 1;
  std::print(
      "Uniform logits: six valid targets, sentence NLL {:.12f}, KL {:.1f}, loss {:.12f}.\n",
      out.nll.item(),
      out.kl.item(),
      out.loss.item());
  const auto ids = tokens.to_vector<int>(), prefix = out.decoder_inputs.to_vector<int>();
  const auto mask = out.mask.to_vector<double>(), loss = out.token_nll.to_vector<double>();
  const auto words = m::SequenceVocabulary();
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(48, 1500);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle st;
  st.width     = 2.4;
  st.height    = 1.5;
  st.font_size = 21;
  d.text({-3, 0}, "Target", 23)
      .text({-3, -2.5}, "Prefix", 23)
      .text({-3, -5}, "Loss mask", 23)
      .text({-3, -7.5}, "Token NLL", 23);
  for (int k = 0; k < 7; ++k) {
    const double x = k * 3.;
    d.node(
         "target" + std::to_string(k), {x, 0}, words[ids[k]] + "\nID " + std::to_string(ids[k]), st)
        .node(
            "prefix" + std::to_string(k),
            {x, -2.5},
            words[prefix[k]] + "\nID " + std::to_string(prefix[k]),
            st)
        .text({x, -5}, std::to_string(int(mask[k])), 23)
        .text({x, -7.5}, k == 6 ? "0" : "log(19)", 23);
  }
  d.save_svg("build/sequence_vae_prefixes.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Uniform logits: six valid targets, sentence NLL 17.666633874999, KL 0.0, loss 17.666633874999.
\image(figures/sequence_vae_prefixes.svg)
// result_end

\caption(BOS enters first, EOS remains a scored target, and only PAD is masked. Uniform-logit NLL sums six log 19 terms; it is not averaged over the seven stored columns.)
\alttext(Aligned target and prefix rows show a one-token shift. The first six masks are one and the last is zero; losses are six log 19 terms and a final zero.)

For each sentence b, the training objective is

$$
\frac 1B\sum_b\left[-\sum_{t:x_{bt}\ne 0}\log p_\theta(x_{bt}\mid x_{b,<t},z_b)
+\frac 12\sum_j(\mu_{bj}^2+e^{l_{bj}}-1-l_{bj})\right].
$$
\alttext(Negative log probabilities sum all non-PAD targets, including EOS, plus coordinate-summed Gaussian KL, then average sentences.)

This is the ordinary negative ELBO with a sampled reconstruction term. Teacher token
perplexity exponentiates total token NLL divided by total non-PAD token count. It conditions
on observed prefixes and a code inferred from the whole sentence, so it is not unconditional
language-model perplexity. Four draws average reconstruction terms for validation/test;
analytic KL is counted once because it does not depend on epsilon.

> Native local grammar and complete explicit fitting

Native sequence-vae-assets exhausts 2 articles×3 colours×3 shapes×2 verbs×4 directions×3
adverb choices=432 unique sentences. The adverb is absent, quickly or slowly. Six/seven
EOS-inclusive target lengths are right-padded to seven. Residue
2*((colour+shape+adverb)%3)+(article+verb+direction)%2 selects test 0, validation 1, fit 2–5:
288/72/72 disjoint combinations with balanced factor marginals. This is procedural teaching
data, not a language benchmark. The loader regenerates every token, previous-target input,
length, factor and source ID. Factors/IDs are audit metadata, never network inputs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto root  = dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("sequence-vae-assets");
  const auto pools = dm::nn::models::LoadSequenceVaeData(root + "/sequence_vae");
  std::print(
      "| pool | rows | valid targets | first source ID | first sentence "
      "|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n");
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const auto& p = pools[k];
    std::print(
        "| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
        k == 0   ? "fit"
        : k == 1 ? "validation"
                 : "test",
        p.tokens.size(0),
        dm::nn::sum(p.lengths).item<int>(),
        p.source.to_vector<int>()[0],
        dm::nn::models::SequenceText(p.tokens, 0));
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| pool | rows | valid targets | first source ID | first sentence |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| fit | 288 | 1920 | 1 | a red circle moves left quickly [eos] |
| validation | 72 | 480 | 3 | a red circle moves right [eos] |
| test | 72 | 480 | 0 | a red circle moves left [eos] |
// result_end

Seed 3109 initializes 22 leaves/3,243 scalars, including separate embedding books. BatchOrder
(288,32,3119) gives nine steps per epoch and 27 total Adam updates. Rate 0.003, moments 0.9/0.999
and epsilon 1e−8 match the source. There is no KL annealing, word dropout, gradient clipping
or free-bit adjustment. Full BPTT, finite/nonzero first-gradient checks and exact zero gradients
for unused/PAD embedding rows remain visible in the program.

Fresh training Gaussian banks use 3192/3193/3194. Fixed four-draw fit/validation/test banks
use 3137/3163/3181. Prior codes use 3203; token uniforms use 3217. The native
MidpointUniformNoise API consumes one MT19937 raw 32-bit word per value, converts it to
(raw+.5)/2^32, and retains Float64 strict-open-interval values. Casting those uniforms to
Float32 could round the upper endpoint to 1; categorical generation receives the original
Float64 bank. Gaussian Float64 banks and Float32 casts are both saved.

All completed epochs 1–3 are eligible, excluding epoch 0. The smallest fixed four-draw
validation negative ELBO selects the checkpoint. Test values never select it. Float32
per-case terms accumulate in Float64, draw then row, retaining source reduction order.
Fresh model-only restore reproduces the selected score; optimizer-resume state is not saved.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <chrono>
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>
#include <map>
namespace nn = dm::nn;
namespace ae {
using nn::models::SequenceDataArrays;
using nn::models::SequenceGeneration;
using nn::models::SequenceGrammarValid;
using nn::models::SequenceText;
using nn::models::SequenceVaeData;
using nn::models::SequenceVaeOutput;
void Require(bool condition, const std::string& why) {
  if (!condition)
    throw std::runtime_error(why);
}
void Near(double x, double y, double tolerance, const std::string& why) {
  Require(std::abs(x - y) <= tolerance, why);
}
nn::Tensor Find(const nn::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& name) {
  for (const auto& [key, t] : a)
    if (key == name)
      return t;
  throw std::runtime_error(name);
}
std::vector<float> Bytes(const nn::Tensor& t) {
  return t.contiguous().to_vector<float>();
}
nn::NamedTensors Arrays(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  nn::NamedTensors out;
  for (const auto& name : p.names())
    out.emplace_back(name, p.at(name).detach().clone());
  return out;
}
auto Snapshot(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  return p.flatten();
}
double MaxAbsDiff(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b, std::int64_t count) {
  const auto x = Bytes(a), y = Bytes(b);
  double     result = 0;
  for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < count; ++i)
    result = std::max(result, std::abs(double(x[i]) - double(y[i])));
  return result;
}
struct VaeNoiseBank {
  nn::Tensor standard, epsilon;
};
VaeNoiseBank BetaVaeNoise(std::int64_t n, std::int64_t k, std::uint32_t seed) {
  auto standard = nn::models::GaussianNoise({n, 4}, k, seed);
  return {standard, nn::cast(standard, nn::DType::Float32)};
}
nn::Tensor BetaVaeNoiseAt(const VaeNoiseBank& b, std::int64_t k) {
  return nn::select(b.epsilon, 0, k).contiguous();
}
inline nn::NamedTensors SequenceFields(const SequenceVaeOutput& o) {
  return {
      {"decoder_inputs", o.decoder_inputs},
      {"encoder_state", o.encoder_state},
      {"encoder_states", o.encoder_states},
      {"mu", o.mu},
      {"log_variance", o.log_variance},
      {"z", o.z},
      {"decoder_initial", o.decoder_initial},
      {"decoder_states", o.decoder_states},
      {"logits", o.logits},
      {"probability", o.probability},
      {"predicted_ids", o.predicted_ids},
      {"mask", o.mask},
      {"token_nll", o.token_nll},
      {"nll", o.nll},
      {"kl", o.kl},
      {"correct", o.correct},
      {"valid_tokens", o.valid_tokens},
      {"loss", o.loss}};
}

void Warm(nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  nn::models::SequenceVariationalAutoencoder(
      p, nn::from_vector(std::vector<int>(7, 3), {1, 7}), nn::zeros({1, 4}));
  Require(p.size() == 22 && p.count() == 3243, "source census22/3243");
}
SequenceVaeOutput
Evaluate(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& tokens, const nn::Tensor& noise) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  auto            out = nn::models::SequenceVariationalAutoencoder(p, tokens, noise);
  for (auto* t :
       {&out.decoder_inputs,
        &out.encoder_state,
        &out.encoder_states,
        &out.mu,
        &out.log_variance,
        &out.z,
        &out.decoder_initial,
        &out.decoder_states,
        &out.logits,
        &out.probability,
        &out.predicted_ids,
        &out.mask,
        &out.token_nll,
        &out.nll,
        &out.kl,
        &out.correct,
        &out.valid_tokens,
        &out.loss}) {
    *t = t->contiguous();
    if (t->dtype() == nn::DType::Float32)
      for (float v : t->to_vector<float>())
        Require(std::isfinite(v), "all18 fields finite");
  }
  return out;
}
nn::models::SequenceGeneration Generate(
    nn::ParameterStore& p,
    const nn::Tensor&   z,
    bool                sample   = false,
    const nn::Tensor&   uniforms = {}) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  return nn::models::SequenceGenerate(p, z, sample, uniforms);
}
std::pair<nn::Tensor, nn::Tensor>
Teacher(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& z, const nn::Tensor& inputs) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  auto            out = nn::models::SequenceTeacher(p, z, inputs);
  return {out.logits.contiguous(), out.probability.contiguous()};
}
std::vector<double>
SequenceVaeScore(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& tokens, const VaeNoiseBank& bank) {
  double     nll = 0, kl = 0, correct = 0, valid = 0;
  const auto n = tokens.size(0), samples = bank.epsilon.size(0);
  for (std::int64_t k = 0; k < samples; ++k) {
    auto       out = Evaluate(p, tokens, BetaVaeNoiseAt(bank, k));
    const auto a = out.nll.to_vector<float>(), c = out.correct.to_vector<float>(),
               v = out.valid_tokens.to_vector<float>(), d = out.kl.to_vector<float>();
    for (std::int64_t b = 0; b < n; ++b) {
      nll += a[b];
      correct += c[b];
      valid += v[b];
      if (k == 0)
        kl += d[b];
    }
  }
  const double m = double(n) * double(samples);
  return {nll / m, kl / n, nll / m + kl / n, std::exp(nll / valid), correct / valid};
}

nn::Tensor ExtraPaddingState(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& tokens) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  return nn::models::SequenceEncoder(p, tokens).state.contiguous();
}
inline nn::NamedTensors CheckGradients(
    const nn::ParameterStore&      store,
    const std::vector<nn::Tensor>& gradients,
    const std::string&             finite,
    const std::string&             nonzero) {
  nn::NamedTensors out;
  Require(gradients.size() == store.size(), "one gradient per parameter");
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < gradients.size(); ++i) {
    Require(gradients[i].defined(), nonzero);
    double norm = 0;
    for (float v : gradients[i].contiguous().to_vector<float>()) {
      Require(std::isfinite(v), finite);
      norm += double(v) * v;
    }
    Require(norm > 0, nonzero);
    out.emplace_back(store.names()[i], gradients[i]);
  }
  return out;
}

} // namespace ae
namespace check {
using ae::Near;
using ae::Require;
} // namespace check
using ae::Require;
namespace {

namespace nn = datamunge::nn;

std::vector<int> GenerationStats(const nn::Tensor& ids) {
  int                   ended = 0, valid = 0;
  std::set<std::string> unique;
  const auto            v = ids.to_vector<int>();
  for (std::int64_t b = 0; b < ids.size(0); ++b) {
    bool done = false;
    for (int t = 0; t < 7; ++t) {
      const int token = v[b * 7 + t];
      check::Require(token >= 0 && token < 19, "generated token in vocabulary");
      if (done)
        check::Require(token == 0, "EOS output suffix must be PAD");
      if (token == 2)
        done = true;
    }
    ended += done;
    valid += ae::SequenceGrammarValid(ids, b);
    unique.insert(ae::SequenceText(ids, b));
  }
  return {ended, valid, int(unique.size())};
}

void Add(nn::NamedTensors& out, const std::string& prefix, const nn::NamedTensors& fields) {
  for (const auto& [key, value] : fields)
    out.emplace_back(prefix + key, value);
}
nn::NamedTensors Fields(const ae::SequenceGeneration& g) {
  return {{"ids", g.ids}, {"logits", g.logits}, {"probability", g.probability}, {"ended", g.ended}};
}

void Run(
    const std::filesystem::path& data,
    const std::filesystem::path& root,
    int                          epochs,
    const std::string&           init) {
  auto pools = nn::models::LoadSequenceVaeData(data.string());
  std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      data / "manifest.json",
      root / "data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      data / "vocabulary.txt",
      root / "vocabulary.txt",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  nn::save_npz((root / "data.npz").string(), ae::SequenceDataArrays(pools));
  std::vector<ae::VaeNoiseBank> noise{
      ae::BetaVaeNoise(288, 4, 3137), ae::BetaVaeNoise(72, 4, 3163), ae::BetaVaeNoise(72, 4, 3181)},
      training;
  auto             prior_noise = ae::BetaVaeNoise(20, 1, 3203);
  nn::NamedTensors fixed{
      {"prior_standard", prior_noise.standard}, {"prior_epsilon", prior_noise.epsilon}};
  for (int split = 0; split < 3; ++split) {
    const std::string name = split == 0 ? "fit" : split == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    fixed.emplace_back(name + "_standard", noise[split].standard);
    fixed.emplace_back(name + "_epsilon", noise[split].epsilon);
  }
  nn::save_npz((root / "fixed_noise.npz").string(), fixed);
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    training.push_back(ae::BetaVaeNoise(288, 1, 3191 + epoch));
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("train_noise_epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + ".npz")).string(),
        {{"standard", training.back().standard}, {"epsilon", training.back().epsilon}});
  }
  nn::ParameterStore model(3109);
  ae::Warm(model);
  nn::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  nn::Optimizer optimizer(model, .003, config);
  if (!init.empty())
    model.load(init);
  check::Require(
      model.count() == 3243 && model.size() == 22,
      "small embedding8/GRU16/latent4 sentence VAE census");
  nn::save_npz((root / "initial_arrays.npz").string(), ae::Arrays(model));
  nn::BatchOrder order(288, 32, 3119);
  std::ofstream  history(root / "history.tsv"), batches(root / "batches.tsv");
  history.precision(17);
  history
      << "epoch\ttrain_preupdate_negative_elbo\tvalidation_sequence_nll\tvalidation_kl\tvalidation_"
         "negative_elbo\t"
         "validation_teacher_reconstruction_token_perplexity\tvalidation_teacher_token_accuracy\n";
  batches << "epoch\tstep\trow\tsource_id\n";
  const auto fit_source = pools[0].source.to_vector<int>();
  const auto best_path  = (root / "best.npz").string();
  double     best       = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
  int        selected = 0, step = 0;
  const auto started = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    order.begin_epoch();
    auto   epsilon = ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(training[epoch - 1], 0);
    double sum     = 0;
    int    seen    = 0;
    for (;;) {
      auto rows = order.next();
      if (rows.empty())
        break;
      auto input = nn::take_rows(pools[0].tokens, rows), e = nn::take_rows(epsilon, rows);
      if (step == 0) {
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_batch.npz").string(), {{"tokens", input}, {"epsilon", e}});
        auto gradients = ae::CheckGradients(
            model,
            nn::grad(
                nn::models::SequenceVariationalAutoencoder(model, input, e).loss,
                model.parameters()),
            "all GRU BPTT gradients finite",
            "all22sentence VAE tensors receive derivatives");
        for (const auto& [name, row] : std::vector<std::pair<std::string, int>>{
                 {"encoder_embedding", 0},
                 {"encoder_embedding", 1},
                 {"decoder_embedding", 0},
                 {"decoder_embedding", 2}})
          for (float v : nn::select(ae::Find(gradients, name), 0, row).to_vector<float>())
            check::Near(v, 0, 0, "PAD/unused BOS or post-EOS embedding gradients exactly zero");
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_gradients.npz").string(), gradients);
        nn::save_npz(
            (root / "first_forward.npz").string(),
            ae::SequenceFields(ae::Evaluate(model, input, e)));
      }
      // All actual learning is visible: forward, sentence objective, full BPTT, Adam.
      const auto net = nn::models::SequenceVariationalAutoencoder(model, input, e);
      sum += double(rows.size()) * net.loss.item<float>();
      const auto gradients = nn::grad(net.loss, model.parameters());
      Require(gradients.size() == 22, "all22 parameter gradients");
      for (const auto& g : gradients)
        for (double v : g.to_vector<double>())
          Require(std::isfinite(v), "finite BPTT derivative");
      optimizer.step(gradients);
      seen += int(rows.size());
      for (auto row : rows)
        batches << epoch << '\t' << step << '\t' << row << '\t' << fit_source[row] << '\n';
      if (step == 0)
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_update_arrays.npz").string(), ae::Arrays(model));
      ++step;
    }
    check::Require(seen == 288, "all288fit sentences once per epoch");
    auto score = ae::SequenceVaeScore(model, pools[1].tokens, noise[1]);
    history << epoch << '\t' << sum / seen;
    for (double value : score)
      history << '\t' << value;
    history << '\n';
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "_arrays.npz")).string(), ae::Arrays(model));
    if (score[2] < best) {
      best     = score[2];
      selected = epoch;
      model.save(best_path); // four-draw validation negative ELBO selects
    }
  }
  const double seconds =
      std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - started).count();

  nn::ParameterStore deployed(3109);
  ae::Warm(deployed);
  deployed.load(best_path); // fresh sentence VAE model-only restore
  check::Near(
      ae::SequenceVaeScore(deployed, pools[1].tokens, noise[1])[2],
      best,
      1e-8,
      "restored selected sequence score");
  const auto       before = ae::Snapshot(deployed);
  nn::NamedTensors output;
  for (int split = 0; split < 3; ++split) {
    const std::int64_t n    = pools[split].tokens.size(0);
    const std::string  name = split == 0 ? "fit" : split == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    auto               mean = ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[split].tokens, nn::zeros({n, 4}));
    check::Require(nn::equal_bits(mean.z, mean.mu), "epsilon0 gives z=mu");
    check::Require(
        nn::equal_bits(mean.decoder_inputs, pools[split].inputs),
        "graph decoder input exactly BOS plus previous target");
    Add(output, name + "_mean_greedy_", Fields(ae::Generate(deployed, mean.z)));
    Add(output, name + "_mean_", ae::SequenceFields(mean));
    const auto lengths = pools[split].lengths.to_vector<int>(),
               tokens  = pools[split].tokens.to_vector<int>();
    for (int k = 0; k < 4; ++k) {
      auto f = ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[split].tokens, ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[split], k));
      check::Require(
          nn::equal_bits(f.mu, mean.mu) && nn::equal_bits(f.encoder_state, mean.encoder_state),
          "Gaussian noise does not change sentence encoding");
      const auto valid     = f.valid_tokens.to_vector<float>(),
                 token_nll = f.token_nll.to_vector<float>();
      for (std::int64_t b = 0; b < n; ++b) {
        check::Near(valid[b], lengths[b], 0, "mask includes EOS,excludes PAD");
        for (int t = 0; t < 7; ++t)
          if (tokens[b * 7 + t] == 0)
            check::Near(token_nll[b * 7 + t], 0, 0, "padding has exactly zero reconstruction loss");
      }
      Add(output, name + "_draw" + std::to_string(k) + "_", ae::SequenceFields(f));
    }
  }
  auto test   = ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].tokens, ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[2], 0)),
       repeat = ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].tokens, ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[2], 0)),
       other  = ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].tokens, ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[2], 1));
  check::Require(
      nn::equal_bits(test.probability, repeat.probability),
      "fixed-noise teacher probabilities repeat bitexact");
  check::Require(
      !nn::equal_bits(test.z, other.z) && !nn::equal_bits(test.probability, other.probability),
      "Gaussian samples affect latent and teacher decoder");
  check::Require(
      nn::equal_bits(ae::Teacher(deployed, test.z, pools[2].inputs).second, test.probability),
      "fixed-z prefix-only decoder exactly matches teacher evaluation");
  auto single = ae::Evaluate(
      deployed,
      nn::take_rows(pools[2].tokens, {0}),
      nn::take_rows(ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[2], 0), {0}));
  const double parity = ae::MaxAbsDiff(single.probability, test.probability, 7 * 19);
  check::Require(parity < 2e-6, "sequence single/batch parity");
  std::vector<int> padded(72 * 8, 0);
  {
    const auto v = pools[2].tokens.to_vector<int>();
    for (int b = 0; b < 72; ++b)
      for (int t = 0; t < 7; ++t)
        padded[b * 8 + t] = v[b * 7 + t];
  }
  auto padded_tokens = nn::from_vector(padded, {72, 8});
  auto extra         = ae::ExtraPaddingState(deployed, padded_tokens);
  check::Require(
      nn::equal_bits(extra, test.encoder_state),
      "appending an extra PAD leaves encoded state BITEXACT");
  nn::save_npz(
      (root / "padding_probe.npz").string(),
      {{"tokens8", padded_tokens}, {"encoder_state8", extra}});

  auto probe_z = nn::take_rows(test.z, {0}), prefix = nn::take_rows(pools[2].inputs, {0});
  auto changed_v = prefix.to_vector<int>();
  changed_v[4]   = changed_v[4] == 5 ? 6 : 5;
  auto changed   = nn::from_vector(changed_v, {1, 7});
  auto original  = ae::Teacher(deployed, probe_z, prefix).first.to_vector<float>(),
       altered   = ae::Teacher(deployed, probe_z, changed).first.to_vector<float>();
  double earlier = 0, later = 0;
  for (int t = 0; t < 7; ++t)
    for (int w = 0; w < 19; ++w) {
      const double delta        = std::abs(double(original[t * 19 + w]) - altered[t * 19 + w]);
      (t < 4 ? earlier : later) = std::max(t < 4 ? earlier : later, delta);
    }
  check::Require(
      earlier == 0 && later > 1e-6,
      "future decoder input cannot affect earlier token logits at FIXED z");
  nn::save_npz(
      (root / "causality_probe.npz").string(),
      {{"z", probe_z},
       {"inputs", prefix},
       {"changed_inputs", changed},
       {"logits", nn::from_vector(original, {1, 7, 19})},
       {"changed_logits", nn::from_vector(altered, {1, 7, 19})}});

  auto prior_z               = ae::BetaVaeNoiseAt(prior_noise, 0),
       token_uniforms        = nn::models::MidpointUniformNoise({20, 7}, 3217);
  auto prior_greedy          = ae::Generate(deployed, prior_z),
       prior_sampled         = ae::Generate(deployed, prior_z, true, token_uniforms);
  auto         zero_gen      = ae::Generate(deployed, nn::zeros({20, 4}));
  const double latent_effect = ae::MaxAbsDiff(prior_greedy.logits, zero_gen.logits, 20 * 7 * 19);
  check::Require(
      latent_effect > 1e-5, "free decoder logits structurally depend on sentence latent");
  auto posterior_greedy = ae::Generate(deployed, test.z);
  Add(output, "test_posterior_greedy_", Fields(posterior_greedy));
  nn::NamedTensors prior{{"z", prior_z}, {"token_uniforms", token_uniforms}};
  Add(prior, "greedy_", Fields(prior_greedy));
  Add(prior, "sampled_", Fields(prior_sampled));
  Add(prior, "zero_", Fields(zero_gen));
  nn::save_npz((root / "prior.npz").string(), prior);
  auto greedy_stats  = GenerationStats(prior_greedy.ids),
       sampled_stats = GenerationStats(prior_sampled.ids);
  GenerationStats(ae::Find(output, "test_mean_greedy_ids"));
  GenerationStats(posterior_greedy.ids);
  check::Require(
      before == ae::Snapshot(deployed),
      "teacher/padding/causality/free generation leave all parameters unchanged");
  nn::save_npz((root / "outputs.npz").string(), output);
  nn::save_npz((root / "model_arrays.npz").string(), ae::Arrays(deployed));

  const auto fit_mask =
      nn::expand_dims(nn::cast(nn::not_equal(pools[0].tokens, 0.), nn::DType::Float32), 2);
  const auto count_tensor =
      nn::cast(nn::sum(nn::one_hot(pools[0].tokens, 19) * fit_mask, {0, 1}), nn::DType::Int32);
  const auto unigram_count = count_tensor.to_vector<int>();
  const int  fit_tokens    = nn::sum(count_tensor).item<int>();
  const auto unigram_probability =
      ((nn::cast(count_tensor, nn::DType::Float64) + .5) / (double(fit_tokens) + 9.5))
          .to_vector<double>();
  double baseline_nll = 0;
  int    test_tokens  = 0;
  for (int token : pools[2].tokens.to_vector<int>())
    if (token) {
      baseline_nll -= std::log(unigram_probability[token]);
      ++test_tokens;
    }
  nn::save_npz(
      (root / "unigram_baseline.npz").string(),
      {{"fit_counts", nn::from_vector(unigram_count, {19})},
       {"probabilities", nn::from_vector(unigram_probability, {19})}});
  auto          score = ae::SequenceVaeScore(deployed, pools[2].tokens, noise[2]);
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta.precision(17);
  meta << "{\"parameters\":3243,\"tensors\":22,\"epochs\":" << epochs << ",\"updates\":" << step
       << ",\"selected_epoch\":" << selected
       << ",\"mc_samples\":4,\"vocabulary\":19,\"maximum_steps\":7,\"test_sequence_nll\":"
       << score[0] << ",\"test_kl\":" << score[1] << ",\"test_negative_elbo\":" << score[2]
       << ",\"test_teacher_reconstruction_token_perplexity\":" << score[3]
       << ",\"test_teacher_token_accuracy\":" << score[4]
       << ",\"fit_only_unigram_test_sequence_nll\":" << baseline_nll / 72
       << ",\"fit_only_unigram_test_token_perplexity\":" << std::exp(baseline_nll / test_tokens)
       << ",\"prior_greedy_eos_count\":" << greedy_stats[0]
       << ",\"prior_greedy_grammar_valid_count\":" << greedy_stats[1]
       << ",\"prior_greedy_unique_count\":" << greedy_stats[2]
       << ",\"prior_sampled_eos_count\":" << sampled_stats[0]
       << ",\"prior_sampled_grammar_valid_count\":" << sampled_stats[1]
       << ",\"prior_sampled_unique_count\":" << sampled_stats[2]
       << ",\"single_batch_max_error\":" << parity << ",\"causal_earlier_max_effect\":" << earlier
       << ",\"causal_later_max_effect\":" << later
       << ",\"latent_generation_logit_max_effect\":" << latent_effect
       << ",\"training_seconds\":" << seconds << "}\n";

  std::ofstream table(root / "examples.tsv");
  table << "case\tsource_id\toriginal\tteacher_argmax\tfree_mean_greedy\tfree_posterior_greedy\n";
  const auto test_source = pools[2].source.to_vector<int>();
  for (int k = 0; k < 10; ++k) {
    const int b     = k * 71 / 9;
    auto      truth = ae::SequenceText(pools[2].tokens, b),
         teacher    = ae::SequenceText(ae::Find(output, "test_mean_predicted_ids"), b),
         free       = ae::SequenceText(ae::Find(output, "test_mean_greedy_ids"), b),
         post       = ae::SequenceText(posterior_greedy.ids, b);
    table << k << '\t' << test_source[b] << '\t' << truth << '\t' << teacher << '\t' << free << '\t'
          << post << '\n';
  }
  std::ofstream prior_table(root / "prior_examples.tsv");
  prior_table << "case\tgreedy\tgreedy_eos\tgreedy_grammar_valid\tsampled\tsampled_eos\tsampled_"
                 "grammar_valid\n";
  const auto greedy_ended  = prior_greedy.ended.to_vector<int>(),
             sampled_ended = prior_sampled.ended.to_vector<int>();
  for (int b = 0; b < 20; ++b) {
    auto g = ae::SequenceText(prior_greedy.ids, b), s = ae::SequenceText(prior_sampled.ids, b);
    prior_table << b << '\t' << g << '\t' << greedy_ended[b] << '\t'
                << ae::SequenceGrammarValid(prior_greedy.ids, b) << '\t' << s << '\t'
                << sampled_ended[b] << '\t' << ae::SequenceGrammarValid(prior_sampled.ids, b)
                << '\n';
  }
  Require(
      bool(meta) && bool(table) && bool(prior_table) && bool(history) && bool(batches),
      "complete sentence VAE evidence");
  std::print(
      "| selected epoch | test sequence NLL | KL | negative ELBO | teacher token PPL | teacher "
      "accuracy | unigram NLL | unigram PPL |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| {} | "
      "{:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",
      selected,
      score[0],
      score[1],
      score[2],
      score[3],
      score[4],
      baseline_nll / 72,
      std::exp(baseline_nll / test_tokens));
}

} // namespace

int main() {
  try {
    const auto cache = dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("sequence-vae-assets");
    Run(std::filesystem::path(cache) / "sequence_vae", "build/sequence_vae", 3, "");
    return 0;
  } catch (const std::exception& e) {
    std::cerr << e.what() << '\n';
    return 1;
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| selected epoch | test sequence NLL | KL | negative ELBO | teacher token PPL | teacher accuracy | unigram NLL | unigram PPL |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 3 | 18.650349945 | 0.030573014 | 18.680922959 | 16.404447576 | 0.204166667 | 18.353152521 | 15.689204717 |
// result_end

The program preserves every original archive, complete history/batch TSVs, exact vocabulary
and provenance JSON. Its fitting-only unigram reference counts only non-PAD fitting targets,
adds 0.5 to each of the 19 vocabulary bins, and normalizes by 1920+9.5. It consumes no held-out
counts. Tensor count/smoothing operations retain the original counts/probabilities exactly;
Float64 token-log accumulation retains the original NLL. This simple unconditional-token
reference is not a claim to match the VAE's structured generative model.

> Learning curve and the stronger reference

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sequence_vae_validation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream f("build/sequence_vae/history.tsv");
  std::string   header;
  std::getline(f, header);
  std::vector<double> epoch, train, validation;
  int                 e;
  double              loss, nll, kl, elbo, ppl, accuracy;
  while (f >> e >> loss >> nll >> kl >> elbo >> ppl >> accuracy) {
    epoch.push_back(e);
    train.push_back(loss);
    validation.push_back(elbo);
  }
  if (epoch.size() != 3)
    return 1;
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines(epoch, train, "train (pre)", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .points(epoch, train, "", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .lines(epoch, validation, "validation (end)", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .points(epoch, validation, "", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .title("Sentence negative ELBO / distinct training and validation measurements")
      .x_label("completed epoch / all three eligible")
      .y_label("nats per sentence")
      .x_ticks({1, 2, 3}, {"1", "2", "3"})
      .save_svg("build/sequence_vae_validation.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/sequence_vae_validation.svg)
// result_end

\caption(Training averages losses before each batch update; validation uses the final epoch weights and fixed four-draw noise. Their different timing/estimators do not support an overfitting claim.)
\alttext(Blue training and red validation negative-ELBO curves decline over three epochs. Validation is measured at epoch-end and selects epoch 3.)

Epoch 3 has test sentence NLL 18.650350, KL 0.030573 and negative ELBO 18.680923 nats/sentence.
Teacher token accuracy is 0.204167. The fitted VAE's teacher token perplexity 16.404448 is worse
than the fitting-only smoothed unigram reference 15.689205; their sentence NLLs are 18.650350
and 18.353153 respectively. Neither conditioning on true prefixes nor fitting a latent path
ensures that this short run beats a simple reference.

> What the causality and PAD controls actually test

At a fixed code, change only the decoder input at zero-based column 4. Earlier logits at
columns 0–3 must remain exactly unchanged. Later logits should change. This tests the causal
prefix decoder. If one instead changed the sentence and re-encoded it, z could change and
influence earlier decoder logits; that is a different experiment.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sequence_vae_causality.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  const auto a    = n::load_npz("build/sequence_vae/causality_probe.npz");
  auto       find = [&](const std::string& key) {
    for (const auto& [k, v] : a)
      if (k == key)
        return v;
    throw std::runtime_error(key);
  };
  const auto x = find("logits").to_vector<float>(), y = find("changed_logits").to_vector<float>();
  std::vector<double> step, effect;
  for (int t = 0; t < 7; ++t) {
    double delta = 0;
    for (int w = 0; w < 19; ++w)
      delta = std::max(delta, std::abs(double(x[t * 19 + w]) - y[t * 19 + w]));
    if (t < 4 && delta != 0)
      return 1;
    step.push_back(t);
    effect.push_back(delta);
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.bars(step, effect, "fixed-z prefix intervention", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, .7)
      .title("Change prefix input4 / fixed code / earlier logits unchanged")
      .x_label("zero-based output step")
      .y_label("maximum absolute logit change")
      .x_ticks(step, {"0", "1", "2", "3", "4", "5", "6"})
      .save_svg("build/sequence_vae_causality.svg");
  std::print(
      "Earlier columns0-3: exact zero effect. Largest later effect {:.12f}.\n",
      *std::max_element(effect.begin(), effect.end()));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Earlier columns0-3: exact zero effect. Largest later effect 0.079681035131.
\image(figures/sequence_vae_causality.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The saved fixed-z probe gives exactly zero earlier effect and a later maximum 0.079681035. A future prefix input does not leak into earlier decoder steps.)
\alttext(Logit-change bars are zero at steps 0–3 and positive at steps 4–6 after only prefix input 4 changes, while the latent code stays fixed.)

Appending an eighth PAD column leaves every final encoder state byte-identical; the saved
padding_probe.npz retains the actual 72-case check. Single-row/batch probabilities agree with
maximum error 0. Fixed-noise calls repeat exactly; changing epsilon changes z and decoder
probabilities while leaving mu and encoder states fixed. A prefix-only teacher decoder from
that same z reproduces full teacher probabilities exactly. All diagnostics leave parameters
unchanged. These are implementation/connectivity checks, not evidence of useful semantics.

> Teacher argmax is not free reconstruction

The following are all ten prespecified held-out rows floor(k*71/9). Teacher argmax uses
true prefixes and z=mu. Free greedy(mu) uses no target prefixes; free posterior greedy uses
one matched posterior draw. Neither free greedy output is a posterior predictive mean.
Repetition, missing roles and special tokens remain visible.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream f("build/sequence_vae/examples.tsv");
  std::string   line;
  std::getline(f, line);
  std::print(
      "| case | source ID | original | teacher argmax / true prefixes | free greedy(mu) | free "
      "posterior greedy |\n|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|\n");
  int count = 0;
  while (std::getline(f, line)) {
    for (char& c : line)
      if (c == '\t')
        c = '|';
    std::print("|{}|\n", line);
    ++count;
  }
  return count == 10 ? 0 : 1;
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| case | source ID | original | teacher argmax / true prefixes | free greedy(mu) | free posterior greedy |
|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|
|0|0|a red circle moves left [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|moves [eos]|
|1|47|a red square rolls down slowly [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|the the moves [eos]|
|2|95|a green circle rolls down slowly [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|a a a [eos]|
|3|141|a green triangle rolls down [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|moves [eos]|
|4|189|a blue square rolls down [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|moves down down [eos]|
|5|234|the red circle rolls up [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|
|6|283|the red triangle rolls up quickly [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|
|7|331|the green square rolls up quickly [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|
|8|379|the blue circle rolls up quickly [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|
|9|428|the blue triangle rolls up slowly [eos]|a a [eos]|a a [eos]|a [eos]|
// result_end

The free mean-code reconstructions repeat “a a [eos]”. Teacher predictions can exploit their
supplied prefixes, so a teacher-reconstruction row cannot be interpreted as a target-free
generation. The model has little training and makes no fluency or semantic-representation
claim.

> All twenty prior cases: greedy versus actual token sampling

Both columns start from the same prior codes z~N(0,I). Greedy chooses argmax at every step;
ancestral token sampling compares each supplied uniform with a Float64 renormalized token
CDF using cdf<=u ties, capped at ID 18. After the first emitted EOS, IDs become PAD. Raw scores
continue for all seven steps. PAD/BOS emitted before EOS and maximum-length/no-EOS failures
are not filtered. Later sampled prefixes are the sampled column's own emitted history.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sequence_vae_prior_counts.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  namespace m     = n::models;
  const auto a    = n::load_npz("build/sequence_vae/prior.npz");
  auto       find = [&](const std::string& key) {
    for (const auto& [k, v] : a)
      if (k == key)
        return v;
    throw std::runtime_error(key);
  };
  std::vector<double> counts_g, counts_s;
  for (const std::string name : {"greedy", "sampled"}) {
    const auto            ids   = find(name + "_ids");
    const auto            ended = find(name + "_ended").to_vector<int>();
    int                   eos = 0, valid = 0;
    std::set<std::string> unique;
    for (int b = 0; b < 20; ++b) {
      eos += ended[b];
      valid += m::SequenceGrammarValid(ids, b);
      unique.insert(m::SequenceText(ids, b));
    }
    auto& counts = name == "greedy" ? counts_g : counts_s;
    counts       = {double(eos), double(valid), double(unique.size())};
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.bars({.84, 1.84, 2.84}, counts_g, "prior greedy", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, .28)
      .bars({1.16, 2.16, 3.16}, counts_s, "prior token sampled", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, .28)
      .x_ticks({1, 2, 3}, {"EOS present", "valid grammar", "distinct texts"})
      .y_limits(0, 26)
      .title("Twenty unfiltered prior cases / different decoding policies")
      .x_label("diagnostic count / uniqueness is number of distinct texts")
      .y_label("count")
      .save_svg("build/sequence_vae_prior_counts.svg");
  std::print(
      "| case | prior greedy | EOS | valid grammar | actual ancestral sample | EOS | valid grammar "
      "|\n|---:|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int b = 0; b < 20; ++b) {
    const auto g  = m::SequenceText(find("greedy_ids"), b),
               s  = m::SequenceText(find("sampled_ids"), b);
    const auto ge = find("greedy_ended").to_vector<int>()[b],
               se = find("sampled_ended").to_vector<int>()[b];
    std::print(
        "| {} | {}{} | {} | {} | {}{} | {} | {} |\n",
        b,
        g,
        ge ? "" : " [MAX7,NOEOS]",
        ge,
        m::SequenceGrammarValid(find("greedy_ids"), b) ? 1 : 0,
        s,
        se ? "" : " [MAX7,NOEOS]",
        se,
        m::SequenceGrammarValid(find("sampled_ids"), b) ? 1 : 0);
  }
  std::print(
      "\nGreedy: EOS {}, grammar {}, distinct {}. Token-sampled: EOS {}, grammar {}, distinct "
      "{}.\n",
      int(counts_g[0]),
      int(counts_g[1]),
      int(counts_g[2]),
      int(counts_s[0]),
      int(counts_s[1]),
      int(counts_s[2]));
}
```
