// result_end

\caption(Greedy ends all 20 cases but produces no grammatical sentence and only 10 distinct texts. Token sampling ends 8/20, also has zero grammatical cases, and yields 18 distinct texts. Distinctness alone is not quality.)
\alttext(Paired count bars show greedy versus sampled: EOS 20 versus 8, valid grammar 0 versus 0, and distinct texts 10 versus 18. The accompanying table preserves every one of the twenty sampled cases.)

Twelve token-sampled cases reach all seven steps without EOS. None of either policy's twenty
prior cases satisfies the grammar. The prior-versus-zero latent intervention changes raw
logits by up to 1.237717271, establishing structural latent dependence; hard prefix changes can
also propagate that difference. This does not establish useful sentence information. Short
training, the stronger unigram reference, repeated reconstructions and unfiltered failures
limit what can be concluded from this single seed.

> Reproduction and independent checks

Run all C++ blocks in order with the matching native library. Preparation uses the canonical
shared cache and records the exact local grammar; no Python preparation or external checkout
is involved. The complete source-derived program preserves all 20 original archives/1,454,190
array values, every history/batch/example TSV, vocabulary and non-timing JSON value. The
optional NumPy development oracle checks all 3,243 first BPTT derivatives and exact first Adam,
all eighteen saved endpoints, all three validation checkpoints, Gaussian banks, prior token
uniforms, greedy/ancestral generation, PAD/causality probes and the unigram reference:

```
python3 scripts/check_sequence_variational_autoencoder.py docs/mepml/examples/nn/2_autoencoders/2.2_variational_autoencoders/build/sequence_vae --json build/nn-report-conversion/sequence_report/oracle.json
```

This checks generated artifacts and does not fit or prepare data. Source initialization,
ordering and floating operation order are retained; external-framework trajectory parity
is not claimed. The editable C++ program is the experiment implementation.
